      "writtenOn": "2025-11-18T20:01:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Likewise, this isn\u0027t really gonna work anyway, so we could just do nothing? (Perhaps the entire init_iommu_hw() could do nothing?)\n\nOr we may be ok with this useless but harmless hypercall here, so we may ignore the return value here (and thus avoid changing the existing code here)?\n\nActually, looks like pKVM will return -EPERM, so iommu_resume() will trigger `WARN(1, \"IOMMU setup failed, DMAR can not resume!\\n\")`? Don\u0027t you see this warning in dmesg after suspend/resume?\n\nOr if we\u0027re lucky and `force_on` is true, it will even trigger a panic?",
      "revId": "978040a1d6f04db1c84e3f7c53f3e5906d4ca138",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
